---
source: crates/pipdock-cli/tests/golden.rs
expression: out
---
{
  "$defs": {
    "Blocker": {
      "description": "The package responsible for holding another one back.\n\nARCHITECTURE §3: the engine's report says *what* was held back; *who* is responsible comes from\ncross-referencing the reverse-dependency graph with each blocker's `Requires-Dist` constraint.\n**If attribution is ambiguous, show the constraint without a culprit rather than guessing.**",
      "properties": {
        "by": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/PkgName"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "description": "The package imposing the constraint, absent when attribution is ambiguous."
        },
        "constraint": {
          "description": "The requirement holding the package back, e.g. `\"requests<2.31\"`.\n\n**Data, not a sentence** — hard invariant 4. Until Slice 0 this carried\n`\"scipy 1.11.4 requires numpy <1.28.0,>=1.21.6\"`, a phrase assembled in Rust, which the\nGUI then wrapped in `\"{{by}} requires {{constraint}}\"` and rendered naming the dependent\n**twice**. Only the CLI looked right, because it prints this field alone. The shape here\nnow matches `BrokenDependent.constraint`, which the guard dialog has always composed\ncorrectly.",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "version": {
          "description": "The installed version of [`Self::by`], when the probe knew it.\n\nSplit out for the same reason [`crate::graph::BrokenDependent`] splits it: the two heads\nphrase this differently — the CLI writes `scipy 1.11.4 requires …` itself, the GUI\ninterpolates `plan.blocker` — and neither can un-join a string Rust joined for it.",
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "constraint"
      ],
      "type": "object"
    },
    "Change": {
      "description": "One line of the preview diff.",
      "properties": {
        "from": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/Version"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "description": "Version before, absent for a fresh install."
        },
        "kind": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/ChangeKind",
          "description": "Which preview section this belongs in."
        },
        "name": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/PkgName",
          "description": "Normalized distribution name."
        },
        "to": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/Version",
          "description": "Version the resolver chose."
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "name",
        "to",
        "kind"
      ],
      "type": "object"
    },
    "ChangeKind": {
      "description": "Which section of the preview a change belongs to (UI-SPEC §4).",
      "oneOf": [
        {
          "const": "upgrade",
          "description": "An installed package moving to a newer version.",
          "type": "string"
        },
        {
          "const": "new-dependency",
          "description": "A package pulled in to satisfy something else.",
          "type": "string"
        },
        {
          "const": "new-install",
          "description": "A package the user explicitly asked to install.",
          "type": "string"
        },
        {
          "const": "downgrade",
          "description": "A package moving to an older version to satisfy a constraint.",
          "type": "string"
        }
      ]
    },
    "HeldBack": {
      "description": "A package the resolver could not take all the way to `latest`.",
      "properties": {
        "blockers": {
          "default": [],
          "description": "Why it could not go further. Empty means the engine gave no attributable reason.",
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/Blocker"
          },
          "type": "array"
        },
        "latest": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/Version",
          "description": "The version the index offers."
        },
        "pkg": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/PkgName",
          "description": "Normalized distribution name."
        },
        "resolved": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/Version",
          "description": "The version the resolver settled on."
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "pkg",
        "resolved",
        "latest"
      ],
      "type": "object"
    },
    "ImpossibleDetail": {
      "description": "A `ResolutionImpossible` outcome and whatever detail the engine gave (`PD-RES-001`).",
      "properties": {
        "explanation": {
          "description": "The engine's own explanation, verbatim.",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "packages": {
          "default": [],
          "description": "Packages involved in the unsatisfiable set.",
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/PkgName"
          },
          "type": "array"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "explanation"
      ],
      "type": "object"
    },
    "PkgName": {
      "description": "A PEP 503-normalized distribution name.\n\nConstructing one is the *only* way a package name reaches an argv array, which is what makes\nSECURITY §2's \"validated before it reaches argv\" claim structural rather than aspirational.",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "PythonMismatch": {
      "description": "A pin the user asked for that cannot install on this environment's Python (`PD-PKG-001`).\n\nHard invariant 10 says PipDock enforces `Requires-Python` itself, because the engines disagree:\npip refuses such a pin with the same \"No matching distribution\" it uses for a typo, and uv\nignores an upper bound and plans it. Structured, not a sentence (invariant 4): the preview shows\nthe required range against the environment's version, and a catalog cannot un-join a string.",
      "properties": {
        "pkg": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/PkgName",
          "description": "The package."
        },
        "python": {
          "description": "The environment's Python, e.g. `\"3.12.4\"`.",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "requiresPython": {
          "description": "That release's `Requires-Python`, verbatim.",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "version": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/Version",
          "description": "The version that was asked for or planned."
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "pkg",
        "version",
        "requiresPython",
        "python"
      ],
      "type": "object"
    },
    "Version": {
      "description": "A version string as the engine reported it. Never reshaped or localized (I18N §2).",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "YankWarning": {
      "description": "A yanked release appearing in a plan.\n\nSP-2: a yank is **not** a failure. Both engines exit 0 and install it, so this is a preview\nwarning row, not an error path (`docs/ERROR-CATALOG.md` PD-PKG-003).",
      "properties": {
        "pkg": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/PkgName",
          "description": "The yanked distribution."
        },
        "reason": {
          "description": "Upstream's stated reason, when given.",
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "version": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/Version",
          "description": "The version that was yanked."
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "pkg",
        "version"
      ],
      "type": "object"
    }
  },
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "description": "The normalized dry-run result.\n\n**Both adapters must emit this same shape** — that is the whole point of the `Engine` trait\n(ARCHITECTURE §3). The pip adapter fills it from `--dry-run --report` JSON; the uv adapter from\nuv's text plan output.\n\nThe exact field set is **provisional until spike SP-1** confirms uv's output is rich enough to\npopulate `held_back.blockers`. If it is not, SP-1's go/no-go says v1.0 ships pip-primary with uv\nbehind a beta flag.",
  "properties": {
    "changes": {
      "default": [],
      "description": "Everything that would change if the user confirms.",
      "items": {
        "$ref": "#/$defs/Change"
      },
      "type": "array"
    },
    "forced": {
      "description": "Packages the user chose to **force** past what installed dependents allow, each with what\nit will break — the \"Will break\" section of the preview (DISCLAIMER §2).",
      "items": {
        "$ref": "#/$defs/HeldBack"
      },
      "type": "array"
    },
    "heldBack": {
      "default": [],
      "description": "Packages that could not reach `latest`, with attribution.",
      "items": {
        "$ref": "#/$defs/HeldBack"
      },
      "type": "array"
    },
    "impossible": {
      "anyOf": [
        {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/ImpossibleDetail"
        },
        {
          "type": "null"
        }
      ],
      "description": "Present when the whole resolution failed."
    },
    "incompatible": {
      "description": "Pins left out because their `Requires-Python` excludes this environment (`PD-PKG-001`).",
      "items": {
        "$ref": "#/$defs/PythonMismatch"
      },
      "type": "array"
    },
    "yanked": {
      "description": "Yanked releases the plan would install. A warning, not a failure (`PD-PKG-003`, SP-2):\nboth engines exit 0 and install them. Both adapters parsed these and then dropped them, so\nthe preview never showed one.",
      "items": {
        "$ref": "#/$defs/YankWarning"
      },
      "type": "array"
    }
  },
  "title": "ResolutionReport",
  "type": "object"
}
